From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: sequencer source (IMFSequencerSource, IMFMediaSourceEx, topology provider)

MFCreateSequencerSource returned an object whose five IMFSequencerSource
methods and GetMediaSourceTopology were E_NOTIMPL with FIXMEs, and that was
not an IMFMediaSource. Written from the public documentation (no conformance
test covers it beyond creation):

- AppendTopology queues topologies in order and hands out unique element ids;
  SequencerTopologyFlags_Last ends the queue (a later append is
  MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST), other flag bits are E_INVALIDARG.
- DeleteTopology, UpdateTopology and UpdateTopologyFlags work on an element
  id (MF_E_NOT_FOUND when unknown); GetPresentationContext and
  GetMediaSourceTopology map a descriptor from CreatePresentationDescriptor
  back to its element id and topology.
- QueryInterface now also gives IMFMediaSourceEx, IMFMediaSource and
  IMFMediaEventGenerator: event queue, characteristics (pause, seek),
  descriptor creation (a copy of the first source node's descriptor tagged
  with the element id), Start (MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_TIME_FORMAT for a non-null
  time format, MESourceStarted), Pause/Stop state transitions
  (MF_E_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION from the stopped state), Shutdown
  (MF_E_SHUTDOWN afterwards), source attributes, no stream attributes.
  No streams are produced: the sequencer reports the idle state only.

Gate: test/mf-sequencer-gate.sh.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/topology.c b/dlls/mf/topology.c
index 572d4d4..f361091 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/topology.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/topology.c
